Yep, very obviously wizard bones. You might consider playing locally
instead of on a "private" server.

> Now, I started as a male wizard with an intelligence value of 18,

Startscumming?

> I already was at XL 9 when I descended to DL 2.

That's taking things *really* slowly. I don't agree with people who
say this is a bad idea because "the randomly generated monsters get
tougher" (the pressure in this direction is pretty light, until you
start getting stuff like mumaks or cockatrices), but you really risk
running out of food (even with hungerless casting).

> (full kit of +127 armor)

Be careful. The AC counter is one byte, so it wraps at -127 to +128.
(+128 AC won't cause you to take more damage, but it will make
basically every monster attack guaranteed.) This isn't normally an
issue ;) Watch the status line.

> One was filled with nymphs,

They respect the E-word AFAIK, and are certainly /oD-able. Shouldn't
have been a problem, unless the first one got the jump on you and took
something important.

If I were to pull this trick, I'd give you Vorpal Blade instead of
Grayswandir. ;)

> the other was full of trolls,

So learn strategies for dealing with them. (I'd suggest wishing for a
wand of polymorph; you could use it on either the trolls or the
corpses.)

> the next one had "just" five water demons, where my wands of death were useless.

You're supposed to bash them quickly. Grayswandir is really powerful
even unenchanted.

> These summoned Juiblex however, which in turn summoned Yeenoghu.

From what I've heard so far, I'm kind of surprised Juiblex didn't
finish you off himself :)

> Crap, so I engraved Elbereth with my Magicbane.

I don't think foocubi respect that.

> After that I found myself surrounded by demons,

The E-word doesn't stop monsters from doing anything harmful besides
attacking in melee. In particular, demons will continue to "gate" each
other etc.

> Why didn't I just ignore the other rooms and continued? I never even came
> much farther than DL 10 and never saw the Rogue level or the quest home.

AFAIK, hostile water demons will do their thing as long as you're on
the level, and Juiblex etc. can teleport, so avoiding that room
wouldn't have helped much. (Knowing HOW they teleport might have
helped a lot, though.)


